A cell made of a value of more than one location holds each part at its own place (#2594, #2580): a helper that writes a cell's list and its elements, called three times, a Dict helper, a Dict cache that a closure run by List.map fills, an undo stack of copies and a closure that inserts into a cell's Dict are each accepted and written in place (ownership-v3-kernel.md §3.4, amended). Its live twin is CellContentsAtTheirPlaceLive.
